        "description": "ALLETE, Inc. is a Duluth, Minnesota-based utility holding company whose businesses include Minnesota Power, Superior Water, Light and Power, ALLETE Clean Energy, BNI Energy, New Energy Equity and other energy infrastructure interests. Its regulated utility footprint is concentrated in Minnesota and Wisconsin, with clean-energy activities across North America. The take-private announced in May 2024 closed on December 15, 2025, and ALLETE survived as a privately held company under Alloy Parent LLC. CPP Investments owns 40% indirectly and Global Infrastructure Partners-managed vehicles own the remaining 60% indirectly, comprising GIP Fund V and the GIP-managed Tower Bridge vehicle. BlackRock is shown only as GIP's parent, not as a separate owner. Regulatory filings in 2026 describe a pending internal reorganization around Minnesota Power, not a completed ownership transfer. No later owner exit or signed platform sale was identified through August 23, 2026.",
